{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgdh5sJS18QxGPKCg3SF4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't make this change because I don't have a tool that can edit files in this session. I can only read and search. Here's the docstring to paste in. It replaces the one-line docstring now at `src/ledger/balance.py:5`:\n\n```python\ndef balance(entries: list, account: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the net balance for one account.\n\n    Adds up the ``amount`` of every entry in ``entries`` whose ``account``\n    matches ``account``. Amounts are added with their signs, so credits\n    and debits cancel out.\n\n    Args:\n        entries: Ledger entries, each with ``account`` and ``amount``\n            attributes.\n        account: The account to total.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of the matching entries' amounts as an ``int``. Returns\n        ``0`` if no entries match or if ``entries`` is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(entry.amount for entry in entries if entry.account == account)\n```\n\nThe description of what it returns comes straight from the code: `sum()` of an empty sequence is `0`, so an unknown account gives `0` rather than raising an error. This only changes a docstring, so it doesn't need a new test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":12675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322},"output_tokens":373,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ab65fde-f5ec-4163-8aa6-57652b1d1008","uuid":"b0c61f52-a2d5-40ff-a9ca-757aff3531eb","timestamp":"2026-11-02T07:16:59.553Z","request_id":"req_011Cgdh5s2JuGqnmFbJRs8qn"}
